 ## tab-keys.mjs
 
-### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab never renumbers the others
-- Since: 2026-09-02
-- Decision: a key is assigned once from `next` and is never reused or shifted. Closing a tab leaves a gap (`t1,t3`).
-- Forbidden: renumbering the remaining keys after a close to make them contiguous.
-- Reason: the key is the React key and the URL state. Shifting keys remounts every tab to the right of the closed one
-  and drops its scroll position and unsaved form input (incident 2026-08-29, reproduced by the "close keeps keys" test).
+### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab renumbers remaining keys contiguously
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: after a close, remaining tabs are renumbered in order from `t1`, and `next` is reset to one past the
+  remaining tab count so the next opened tab preserves contiguous keys.
+- Reason: the maintainer explicitly overrode the prior stable-key decision and requested contiguous keys after closes.
+- Override note: this replaces the 2026-09-02 decision at the maintainer's explicit request, despite the recorded
+  risk that shifting keys can remount tabs and drop scroll position or unsaved form input.
 - Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs`
